**10. Ignored / Disabled Test** — `disabledTest()` (line 109)

The `@Disabled("flaky, fix later")` reason gives no tracking reference. This test will rot indefinitely.

```java
@Disabled("flaky, fix later")
```

**Fix:** Either fix the flakiness now (the test logic is trivial and correct) or link a tracking issue:
```java
@Disabled("Flaky: tracked by JIRA-1234")
```
In this case the test body is straightforward — the right move is to remove `@Disabled` and let it run.

